# Testing requirements

Use commands from **`docs/project/setup.md`** and the **Makefile** when present — do not assume scripts that are not in the repo yet.

See **`.cursor/agents/generator.md`** and **`.cursor/rules/code-review.mdc`**.

---

## Coverage expectation

Aim for **~80%** on new/changed **logic** (Go packages, `web/lib`, hooks) once coverage tooling exists. UI-only token tweaks may skip new tests when nothing behavioral changed — say so in the handoff.

---

## Test layers

| Layer | Scope | Tooling |
|--|--|--|
| **Unit** | Pure Go, renderers, RBAC helpers, route-param parsing, formatters | `go test ./...` |
| **Integration** | Docker API, reconcile, Caddy load, deploy state machine | `go test -tags=integration` (Docker required) |
| **Web unit/component** | React hooks, form validation, API client helpers | Vitest/Playwright component tests when added under `web/` |
| **E2E** | Install script, setup, deploy fixture app, critical UI flows | `e2e/` Playwright + shell (briefing §14.2) |
| **UI contract** | New/changed dashboard screens | Structure vs `design-index.json` + Playwright flows — [dockyrd-design-contract](dockyrd-design-contract.mdc) |

---

## SQLite migrations (control plane)

When changing **`internal/db/migrations/`** or sqlc queries:

- Run `go test ./internal/db/...` (or project equivalent).
- Apply migrations on a clean DB in tests or `make test` — forward-only in production.
- Invoke **`database-reviewer`** on non-trivial schema changes (constraints, secrets columns, auth tables).

User **Postgres/Redis** services are provisioned by dockyrd in Docker — not migrated via app Drizzle. E2E fixtures may use Prisma/Drizzle in **sample apps only** under `e2e/fixtures/`.

---

## CI

Briefing §14.3 expects **`.github/workflows/`** (`ci.yml`, `e2e.yml`, `release.yml`). Maintain workflows when adding gates (Go lint, `pnpm` web build, Radix check, integration on main/nightly).

Local runs should mirror CI subsets for touched surfaces — full matrix before release / `push-to-main`.

---

## Radix guard (web)

After dependency changes in `web/`:

```bash
./scripts/check-no-radix.sh
```

Must pass before merge — use Base UI primitives only.

---

## TDD workflow

For behavioral work:

1. **RED** — failing test for the desired behavior  
2. **Run** — confirm failure for the right reason  
3. **GREEN** — minimal fix  
4. **Run** — relevant packages green  
5. **Refactor** — without semantic change  

---

## Review integration

**`code-reviewer`** may spot-check tests; trust generator-reported gates unless suspicious. Keep tests deterministic (fixed time, no flaky sleeps).
